dmtrkrsnr@gmail.com writes:

> -What does elven dagger (+2) mean? What are those numbers near the
> weapon names?

The number with a + or - sign is enchantment. 
Weapons with a higher enchantment are generally better than same kind of
weapons with a lower enchantment.
So, a +2 elven dagger is better than a +1 or +0 elven dagger, but this
doesn't show whether or not it is better than a +1 long sword, because
long swords are different weapons.

You don't usually see the enchantment of all weapons, only that of fully
identified ones.

